models=[('Example2.32 full shifted support classification',r'\partial |x-y|=\begin{cases}\{1\}&x>y\\[-1,1]&x=y\\\{-1\}&x<y\end{cases}','At a match the entire interval [-1,1] is valid, including nonzero supports. Helpers extend to every real x,y, as an explicit stronger global identity.','Arbitrary real x,y; global supporting inequality against every real comparison point.','The full support set, not only one selected sign.','example_2_32_subdifferential'),('Actual projected source update',r'X_{t+1}=\min\{1,\max\{0,X_t-\eta_tG(f_t,X_t)\}\}','This is the existing nearest-point projection applied to the actual chosen current support. No zero tie is assumed.','The clamp identity allows any real eta,x,y. For source-valid runs X0 and labels lie in [0,1] and played eta is positive.','Same actual canonical current-choice OSD trajectory, output before observing label.','loss_step_clamp'),('Example2.32 known-horizon guarantee',r'\eta=1/\sqrt T,\quad\sum_{t=1}^T(|x_t-y_t|-|u-y_t|)\le\sqrt T\quad(\forall u\in[0,1])','Diameter and every actual support norm are at most1. The same eta and trajectory serve every comparator; there is no assumed one-step regret inequality.','T>=1, externally prescribed feasible x1, every played label in [0,1]; no stochastic or independence assumption.','Finite real absolute-loss regret of this same horizon-tuned run.','example_2_32'),('Additional one-sided average corollary',r'\forall\epsilon>0,\quad R_T^{(\eta=1/\sqrt T)}(u)/T<\epsilon\quad\text{eventually in }T','The finite source bound divided by positive T is at most1/sqrt(T), which tends to0. This states an upper epsilon condition, not signed convergence of regret to0.','All labels in [0,1], fixed feasible x1,u, epsilon>0; a separate prescribed eta is used for each T.','Only eventual upper control of the horizon-family average; no absolute-value or anytime bound.','example_2_32_average_eventually')]
