reading={'slug':SLUG,'primary':{'title':'Online Learning: A Modern Introduction Using Convex Optimization','authors':'Francesco Orabona','edition':'arXiv:1912.13213v10,21June2026','sections':'Example2.32 with original guessing game and explicit Algorithm2.2/Theorem2.13 transfer','pages':'printed1-3,15,19-20/PDF13-15,27,31-32','pdf_page':32,'url':URL},'notation':[{'term':'Matched label','meaning':'Partial |x-y| at x=y is the full [-1,1]. Canonical choice is proved to belong to it, not to equal0.'},{'term':'Known horizon and all comparators','meaning':'T>=1 prescribes eta=1/sqrt(T) before one run. Its outputs and current supports do not depend on u. All u in [0,1] satisfy the same real absolute-loss regret bound.'},{'term':'One-sided average family','meaning':'The eventual upper epsilon result uses separately prescribed horizons. It does not assert signed regret/T tends to0 or a single anytime schedule.'}],'algorithm':{'title':'Output, reveal label, choose support, clamp','kind':'source algorithm instance','steps':[{'title':'Output first','detail':'Initialize feasible X0=x1. Xt is determined by strict past labels/steps; output it before y_t is revealed.'},{'title':'Use the actual current loss','detail':'After reveal, f_t(x)=|x-y_t| is proper and globally supported. Full three-case classification proves the actual chosen support has norm<=1, including every tie choice.'},{'title':'Clamp the genuine update','detail':'Use the shared projection of Xt-eta*g_t onto [0,1]. The public identity identifies it with min(1,max(0,...)).'}],'pseudocode':{'title':'Absolute-loss projected OSD for a prescribed horizon','intro':'This is one permitted canonical support choice for Example2.32, with source labels revealed after each output.','formula_label':'True recurrence and fixed tuning','math':r'X_0=x_1\in[0,1],\quad\eta=1/\sqrt T,\quad g_t\in\partial|X_t-y_t|,\quad X_{t+1}=\Pi_{[0,1]}(X_t-\eta g_t)','fallback':'Output the current point, reveal the label, choose its actual global support, and clamp the update to [0,1].','lines':['Prescribe T>=1, feasible x1, and eta=1/sqrt(T).','Initialize X0=x1.','For zero-based t<T, output the already determined Xt.','Reveal y_t in [0,1] and pay |Xt-y_t|.','Choose the canonical current-loss support gt; at Xt=y_t the complete interval [-1,1] is legal.','Set X(t+1)=min(1,max(0,Xt-eta*gt)).'],'relationship':'Strict-prefix equality, support correctness, actual projection, and the same-trajectory all-comparator source guarantee are proved in the shared library. No comparator or future labels are input to the selector; external initialization/tuning are prescribed.'}},'teaching_route':[NS+x for x in preview],'source_theorems':cards,'proof_bridge':{'title':'Translated supports to a real regret producer','summary':'Translate the entire absolute-value subdifferential and instantiate the existing actual OSD tuned bound.','steps':[{'title':'Translate every supporting inequality','detail':'Testing z+y in one direction and z-y in the other gives equality of the entire global support set. The three full absolute-value sets therefore give the shifted source identity.','math':r'\partial|x-y|=\partial|\cdot|(x-y)','fallback':'No affine-inclusion shortcut loses the reverse inclusion.'},{'title':'Produce supports and norm bounds','detail':'Every loss is a finite proper absolute value. Full three-case sets give nonempty supports and ||g||<=1 for every actual support; choose_spec connects the current selector to this bound.','math':r'g\in\partial|x-y|\Rightarrow |g|\le1','fallback':'The match case retains all supports in [-1,1].'},{'title':'Tune the same recurrence','detail':'Feasible points have pairwise distance<=1. Instantiate the shared OSD theorem at D=G=1,T>0 on the actual recursively projected trajectory; finite EReal conversion gives real absolute losses.','math':r'R_T(u)\le\sqrt T','fallback':'The source-valid label premise remains explicit even though the global Lipschitz helper proves a stronger bound.'},{'title':'Only an upper average corollary','detail':'Divide the finite source bound by T>0 and use sqrt(T)/T=1/sqrt(T). Tendsto of the reciprocal supplies eventual epsilon upper control.','math':r'R_T^{(T)}(u)/T\le1/\sqrt T','fallback':'Signed convergence, absolute BigO and anytime behavior are not asserted.'}],'boundary':boundary},'worked_example':{'title':'An actual four-round nonsmooth run','intro':'Alternating labels0,1,0,1 with x1=1 and eta=.5 force nonzero unique supports at all four played outputs.','steps':[{'title':'Computed from the real recurrence','detail':'The true canonical selected supports are1,-1,1,-1, so outputs are1,.5,1,.5,1. Against u=.5, played losses total3 and comparator losses total2.','math':r'R_4(1/2)=1','fallback':'All choices and outputs are proved, not supplied as premises.'},{'title':'Positive terminal and exact fixed bound','detail':'Energy is4, initial-distance contribution1/4, terminal subtraction1/4, and fixed RHS is exactly1. Eta=.5 equals the source-optimal1/sqrt(4); every comparator satisfies the source coarse bound2.','math':r'\frac14+\frac14\cdot4-\frac14=1','fallback':'The exact fixed bound retains a nonzero terminal distance.'},{'title':'True clipping and strict-prefix causality','detail':'Starting at1/4 with label1 and eta1 gives actual support-1, raw5/4 and projection1. Separately, replacing labels from time4 by999 and steps by-99 leaves the past outputX4 unchanged.','math':r'\Pi_{[0,1]}(5/4)=1','fallback':'Invalid future data are used only to test prefix causality, not source-valid performance.'}],'takeaway':'A faithful support producer connects the source nonsmooth example to an actual projected algorithm and its real regret.','boundary':boundary}}
